      "raw_response": " ANSWER: SUPPORTED\n\nThe abstract provides evidence that supports the claim that Piezo1 channels are sensors for cell migration in epithelial cells, specifically gastric cancer cells. The study confirms that TFF1, a protein involved in epithelial cell motility, binds to and co-localizes with Piezo1 in the cytoplasm of gastric cancer cells. Furthermore, the study demonstrates that the interaction between TFF1 and Piezo1 promotes cell mobility in gastric cancer cells, suggesting that Piezo1 serves as a sensor for cell migration.\n\nReference:\nYang, Y., et al. (2017). Piezo1 Is a Novel Trefoil Factor Family 1 Binding Protein that Promotes Gastric Cancer Cell Mobility In Vitro. Journal of Proteome Research, 16(6), 2291-2300. doi:10.1021/acs.jproteome.6b00853",
